 "summary": "Silicon PIN photodiode with a 7.5 mm² radiant sensitive area, in a clear plastic top-view body measuring 5.4 × 4.3 × 3.2 mm with two through-hole leads. It is sensitive from 430 to 1100 nm (peak 900 nm), covering visible and near-infrared light, with a ±65° half-sensitivity angle, and is intended as a high-speed photodetector. At 5 V reverse bias and 1 mW/cm² (950 nm) the reverse light current is 50 µA typ; rise and fall times are 100 ns at 10 V into 1 kΩ. BPW34S is the BPW34 packed in tubes rather than bulk; the part is lead-free and RoHS compliant.",
